1
00:00:03,175 --> 00:00:11,565
Get a pre-authorization approved — Billing ▸ Pre-Authorizations — Request approval before the service, and track it to a decision.

2
00:00:16,847 --> 00:00:22,400
Billing ▸ Pre-Authorizations is where you ask a payer to agree before you deliver the service.

3
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:29,728
Every request sits here with its status — pending waiting on the payer, approved good to go, denied needs another route.

4
00:00:29,728 --> 00:00:40,867
Get this wrong and the work is already done when the refusal arrives. That is why it lives before the visit.

5
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:47,666
Pick the patient — the request carries their insurance across automatically.

6
00:00:47,666 --> 00:00:57,596
Describe the service in the payer’s language, not shorthand. A vague description is a slow decision.

7
00:00:57,596 --> 00:01:11,973
The diagnosis is why the service is needed — searched from the code set, never typed from memory.

8
00:01:11,973 --> 00:01:22,119
The estimated cost sets expectations for the patient as well as the payer.

9
00:01:22,119 --> 00:01:33,081
This box is the one a reviewer reads. Say what you already tried — that is what turns pending into approved.

10
00:01:33,081 --> 00:01:37,362
Submitted. It joins the queue as pending while the payer reviews it.

11
00:01:37,362 --> 00:01:43,815
When it comes back approved you get an authorization number — that number goes on the claim, or the claim gets denied.

12
00:01:43,916 --> 00:01:59,026
What you just did

13
00:01:59,624 --> 00:02:08,624
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
